cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "swatplus-hmscal: Hierarchical Multiscale Calibration (HMSCal) of SWAT+ guided by Adaptive Sensitivity Analysis"
abstract: >-
  HMSCal is an R-based framework for hierarchical multiscale calibration of
  SWAT+ hydrological models. Couples Morris (LH-OAT) sensitivity screening
  re-executed at each temporal scale (annual water balance, monthly
  streamflow, daily streamflow) with sigma-informed parameter-range
  narrowing and cross-iteration filtering to manage equifinality. A runoff
  coefficient target and a multisite aquifer partition proxy stay active
  across every iteration, so the accepted ensemble is constrained on
  internal flow partitioning and not on outlet streamflow alone.
  Built on top of SWATrunR.
